{
  "name": "Kiron Labs - BarMon - Facebook Content v1",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -600,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## BarMon — Facebook Caller v1 (v2)\n\nThin, client-owned workflow: schedule + this profile/channel's config, calls the shared Engine, then handles EVERYTHING client-specific with its own credentials — Telegram send, buttons, and the Sheets update that records the Telegram message id. The Engine itself never touches Telegram (see the Engine's own Sticky Note for why: n8n binds credentials per node at design time, so a shared node can't dynamically switch to 'whichever client's bot').\n\n**Before activating:**\n1. `spreadsheet_id` already set to BarMon's real Google Sheet (19VRjs_zOnaTmHaFqSDIXKMnU5gVccBD7zP0Wx4Z8de0) — nothing to fill in here. Note: the `profile` column was removed from `BarMon-Content` (2026-08-20, redundant now that each client has its own file) — the Engine's Sheets-append node maps columns explicitly and no longer writes a profile value.\n2. Fill in `telegram_chat_id` (BarMon's own review chat, from BarMon's own bot).\n3. Leave `dry_run = true` until drafts look right — dry run only sends a Telegram preview, nothing is logged to Sheets (matches the Engine's contract).\n4. Re-select the Engine workflow in the `Call Content Curation Engine` node after import (ships with a placeholder id).\n\n**Credentials needed:**\n- `Telegram - BarMon` — BarMon's own bot token, used for every Telegram node in this Caller.\n- `Google Sheets - Rob` — reused (same automation Google account as the Engine); needed here only for the final 'save telegram_message_id' update.\n- `Telegram - Rob` — ops channel, used only by this Caller's own Error Trigger branch (failures in scheduling/config/invocation, not inside the Engine)."
      }
    },
    {
